{"choices":[{"finish_reason":"tool_calls","index":0,"message":{"content":"I have strong evidence about Chigozie Obioma (born in Akure, Nigeria; both novels shortlisted for the Booker Prize, translated into 30 languages). But the Booker Prize was established in 1969, not the 2000s. The puzzle says \"the award itself\" was \"originally created in the 2000s.\" Let me reconsider whether the puzzle might involve a different award, or whether I'm misreading the structure.\n\nLet me re-read the puzzle carefully:\n- Book A: contender for an award (the award itself created in the 2000s), translated into 25+ languages\n- In the 2010s, in the year Book A was published, another book (Book B, released the preceding year) won \"the very award above for which the first book was later in contention\"\n- Author of Book B was born in the same city where Author of Book A grew up\n- Question: where was Author of Book A born?\n\nThe phrase \"the very award above for which the first book was later in contention\" suggests the SAME award. So the award was created in the 2000s. The Man Asian Literary Prize (2007) fits. Let me check if Obioma's books were contenders for the Man Asian Literary Prize, and verify the connection. Let me search for the Man Asian Literary Prize Wikipedia page directly.","role":"assistant","tool_calls":[{"function":{"arguments":"{\"queries\": [\"Man Asian Literary Prize\", \"Man Asian Literary Prize winners list\", \"Man Asian Literary Prize 2010 2011 2012 2013 2014 2015\"], \"top_k\": 10}","name":"search"},"id":"call_7b76593a677b4997a2c2872a","index":0,"type":"function"}]}}],"created":1789479389,"id":"chatcmpl-a197b606-e95e-9b7d-9707-3133dbecf6b9","model":"glm-5.2","object":"chat.completion","usage":{"prompt_tokens":17914,"completion_tokens":335,"reasoning_tokens":0,"total_tokens":18249,"cached_tokens":3328,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":3328},"prompt_cost":0.000000,"completion_cost":0.000000,"cache_cost":0.000000}}